# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CaterKart — Vite/React SPA + NestJS API (Prisma/Postgres + Mongo) + AWS CDK
#
# The repo-wide rules. Patterns without a leading slash match at any depth, so
# `node_modules/` covers server/, infra/ and anything added later; a leading
# slash anchors to the repo root on purpose.
#
# Two scoped files stay alongside this one, because their rules would be
# actively wrong applied repo-wide:
#   infra/.gitignore   ignores `*.js` (CDK compiles TS in place) with negations
#                      for the two .js/.sh files that ARE source. Repo-wide that
#                      would swallow the entire frontend.
#   server/.gitignore  ignores .env.production and .swiggy-tokens.json, the
#                      live Swiggy grant written by tools/swiggy.mjs.
# The secret-file patterns below duplicate the server ones deliberately: a
# credential should have to get past two independent rules to be committed.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Dependencies ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
jspm_packages/
bower_components/
.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# Lockfiles are COMMITTED — a reproducible install is the point of them.
# Listed here so nobody adds them back by reflex.
# package-lock.json
# yarn.lock
# pnpm-lock.yaml

# ── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
dist-ssr/
build/
out/
.output/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Vite / bundler caches
.vite/
.rollup.cache/
.parcel-cache/
.turbo/
.swc/

# ── Environment & secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only the *.example templates are tracked. A real env file holds the Swiggy
# token-encryption key, the session signing secret and the Razorpay keys — any
# one of which, committed, means rotating credentials and rewriting history.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
!.env.sample

# Credentials, keys and certificates
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cer
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
.npmrc
.netrc
secrets.json
credentials.json
gha-creds-*.json

# A live Swiggy OAuth grant, written by server/tools/swiggy.mjs during manual
# API exploration. Committing it publishes a token that can place real orders.
.swiggy-tokens.json

# Cloud provider state
.aws/
.aws-sam/
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraformrc

# ── AWS CDK (infra/) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Synthesised templates and asset staging — regenerated by `cdk synth`.
cdk.out/
.cdk.staging/
# `cdk deploy --outputs-file` writes account-specific resource names and
# occasionally endpoint URLs. infra/.gitignore already excludes it; repeated
# here so a copy written elsewhere in the tree is caught too.
cdk-outputs.json

# ── Prisma ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The generated client. `prisma generate` rebuilds it, and it is platform- and
# version-specific — committing it is how CLI/client version skew hides.
server/prisma/generated/
**/.prisma/
# Migrations ARE committed; `migrate deploy` applies exactly these at boot.

# ── Testing & coverage ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
*.lcov
.nyc_output/
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/
junit.xml

# ── Logs & diagnostics ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
report.*.json
*.heapsnapshot
pids/
*.pid
*.seed
*.pid.lock

# ── Local data & scratch ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Docker volumes, database dumps and ad-hoc scratch files. A dump of the
# production database is the single worst thing this repo could contain.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.dump
*.sql.gz
/data/
/tmp/
/scratch/
.cache/

# ── Editors & IDEs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.history/

# VS Code: share the project's recommendations and tasks, keep personal
# settings and launch configs out.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.shared.json
!.vscode/tasks.json

# Agent / assistant local state
.claude/settings.local.json

# ── Operating system ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Icon?
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk
